      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14270613/assets/c735021e606b4f8430784545870d0a26b8c30614dbae3d4cdeeb8871fd97cf21.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find $|a|.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14270613/assets/ad1deeaafc4ca2d9e3f2223f07a91dfdd99ba45558e82face513837217247c20.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$ we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=20\\,\\text{mm}$ and $BH=50\\,\\text{mm}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{20}^{2}+{50}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2\\,900} \\\\  & =10\\sqrt{29}\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
