    "q-118919": {
      "dom_id": "step-q118919",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14270613/assets/a664697bf5760f9b09ab8de9364e5fe2b755c37f8904fad9c9b93985d121cad4.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find $|a|.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14270613/assets/b3c9885d3d620e42f08fc72869c6b063984a01da6b9b5ab9859c5ea7b79df2fc.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$ we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=30\\,\\text{mm}$ and $BH=15\\,\\text{mm}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{30}^{2}+{15}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1\\,125} \\\\  & =15\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
